LIT Bible — Licensing
=====================

This repository holds three kinds of material. Two are the project's own,
under two different licenses; the third is work by others, and other files
that neither license covers, each under its own terms.

1. SOFTWARE — the website's source code (Astro components, layouts, scripts,
   styles, build tooling, configuration). Licensed under the MIT License
   (full text below). You may copy, modify, and reuse it freely, including
   for commercial purposes.

2. CONTENT — the Liberation and Inclusion Translation (LIT) scripture text,
   footnotes, book introductions, glossary entries, and articles. Licensed
   under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0
   International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0). You may share it with attribution, but
   NOT sell it and NOT distribute altered versions.
   The license owner also grants additional permissions (any amount for
   noncommercial use, blanks in teaching handouts, quotation in commercial
   works within limits). They are set out at https://litbible.net/read#license-terms
   and apply in addition to CC BY-NC-ND 4.0.
   Summary:    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/
   Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode
   See also the license notice at https://litbible.net/read#license

Which files are CONTENT (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0), not SOFTWARE:
  - src/data/chapters/            (scripture chapter text)
  - src/data/intros/              (book introductions)
  - src/content/articles/         (articles)
  - src/content/glossary/         (glossary entries)
  - src/data/translation-commitments.json
  - any LIT translation text or editorial prose wherever else it appears

3. OTHER MATERIAL — work by others that the site builds on, and a few files
   of the project's own that are under neither license above. Neither the
   MIT grant nor the CC BY-NC-ND grant extends to any of it. Each item below
   names the notice that states its terms; where a notice gives terms per
   directory or per entry, the notice governs.

Which files are OTHER MATERIAL, not SOFTWARE and not CONTENT:
  - public/greek/                 The Greek New Testament data behind the
    Study Desk's Greek tab and the Greek search: the SBL Greek New Testament
    (SBLGNT), MorphGNT, MACULA Greek, the UBS Greek New Testament Dictionary,
    and lexicons from STEPBible (Tyndale House Cambridge) with text from the
    Perseus Digital Library. These are under Creative Commons Attribution
    (CC BY) and Attribution-ShareAlike (CC BY-SA) licenses of several
    versions; which license applies to which directory, and to which
    entries within a directory, is stated in public/greek/LICENSE.txt, and
    that notice governs. Nothing from the LIT is in these files.
  - src/data/alignment-words/     Each record quotes the Greek words it
    aligns, taken from the SBLGNT as MorphGNT tokenizes it; see the text/
    section of public/greek/LICENSE.txt for both sources' terms. The LIT
    verse text in the same files is CONTENT.
  - public/fonts/text-critical-signs.otf
    Six glyphs subset from Cardo, copyright David J. Perry. SIL Open Font
    License 1.1; notice: public/fonts/text-critical-signs-OFL.txt
  - public/fonts/bracket-markers.otf
    Two glyphs subset from Noto Sans Math, copyright Google LLC. SIL Open
    Font License 1.1; notice: public/fonts/bracket-markers-OFL.txt
  - scripts/og/fonts/*.ttf        Fraunces and Inter, used to draw the share
    cards. SIL Open Font License 1.1; notice: scripts/og/fonts/OFL.txt, with
    the sources in scripts/og/fonts/README.md
  - src/data/podcast-feed.xml     A snapshot of the Found in Translation
    podcast's RSS feed as its host serves it. The podcast's own copyright
    notice, carried in the file, applies.
  - public/images/, public/assets/, _source-images/, and the favicon and
    app-manifest icons at the top of public/
    The site's images. Those that are the project's own (the emblem,
    wordmark, app icon, and screenshots of the apps) are not licensed for
    reuse by this file. The rest are photographs and artwork from other
    sources, used under those sources' own terms; IMAGE-CREDITS.md lists
    each one's source, creator and terms.

Packages installed from npm (the @fontsource font faces, simple-icons, and
the rest of package.json) are not in this repository, though the build
copies parts of some into the site. Each keeps the license in its own
package.

Everything not listed under CONTENT or OTHER MATERIAL is SOFTWARE under the
MIT License. The MIT grant below extends to neither the CONTENT nor the
OTHER MATERIAL.

